    -> sum converges for every a (term_n ~ (beta/2)^n (n+1) e^{a n}/n! : factorial wins).
    NOTE: RHS_A(n) is INCREASING in beta for every n (see [1A]) -> the bound is TIGHTEST
          at small beta, LOOSEST at beta=2.5.  'beta small => RHS small => keep small |r|'
          has the sign of the beta-dependence inverted; and the bound never truncates |r|.
